CJK FONTS

The Adafruit GFX fonts only cover ISO-8859-1, so locales with CJK text (see
LOCALE_USES_CJK_* in platformio/include/cjk_text.h) draw non-Latin-1
characters from separate bitmap fonts. To save flash, those fonts only contain
the characters that are actually used.

Regenerate the fonts after changing any string in locale_zh_CN.inc or
config.cpp (e.g. CITY_STRING):
  python3 gen_cjk_fonts.py

This scans the string literals of those files (plus extra_chars.txt, if
present), downloads the source fonts into ./cache on first run, and writes the
headers to platformio/lib/esp32-weather-epd-assets/fonts/cjk/.

Characters missing from the generated fonts are drawn as blank space.

Which CJK font is used with each Latin font size is set by CJK_FONT_PAIRS in
platformio/src/renderer.cpp. Font sizes and sources are set by FONTS and
SOURCES in gen_cjk_fonts.py.

Dependencies:
  Python 3, Pillow

PREVIEW

  bash preview/run_preview.sh

Compiles platformio/src/cjk_text.cpp for the host together with the generated
fonts, runs a few checks, and renders sample strings to preview/preview.png
(and preview_3x.png). Requires a C++17 compiler.

LICENSES

  Fusion Pixel Font   SIL OFL v1.1   https://github.com/TakWolf/fusion-pixel-font
  Noto Sans SC        SIL OFL v1.1   https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk
